WEBVTT

00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:14,180
Why do some people think that the COVID shot can cause cancer?

00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:23,860
Because it can. So the COVID-19 shot has been showed through numerous studies

00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:32,980
to increase one risk, one's risk for cancer. I cannot tell you how many people that we've had

00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:39,780
called our office that said they were just diagnosed with cancer. It was not long after they had

00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:46,980
the COVID-19 vaccination or booster or that their cancer came back with the vengeance after

00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:54,340
when it was in revision for a number of years after they got the vaccine. There's a lot of data

00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:59,780
out there. I won't go into that anymore. If you really want to search that data, there's research

00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:08,900
articles that have been buried, that do show that increased incidence of cancer and what are

00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:15,860
called turbo cancers. They've been termed turbo cancers because they can they can be very, very

00:01:15,860 --> 00:01:24,740
fast growing cancers that nobody can seem to put the brakes on. There's also evidence that the

00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:36,340
COVID vaccine contained SV-40 as one of the components of the vaccine, which is known cancer-causing

00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:47,060
particle that is used in laboratories to produce cancer in lab rats in order to test different

00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:54,100
medications against it. So they'll give a lab rat SV-40 in order to produce cancer so that they can

00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:59,140
test their chemotherapy against that cancer. Why would you put it in the COVID shot? Are there

00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:08,740
nefarious reasons for all these things? Yeah, well, probably. So I've said way back when COVID came out

00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:17,860
that you did not want to get that vaccine.

